# One real personal identifier per line — checked as a literal
# byte-string substring by check_privacy.py, both across the current
# working tree and the full git history (git cat-file, not git log -p,
# so this also catches a binary blob committed and later removed).
#
# Copy this file to .privacy-tokens and fill in your own values.
# .privacy-tokens itself MUST stay gitignored — never commit it, it's
# the token list, and a script whose own source (or token file) embeds
# the personal data it's checking for would fail on itself forever.
#
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.

# Full name
# Surname alone
# Personal email
# Any handle that identifies you (LinkedIn, etc.)
# Phone, as written
# Phone, digits only, no formatting
# Home town / specific location
# Former employer names exactly as they appear in your CV/config —
#   use the full division/entity string, not a bare company name, since
#   a bare name may legitimately appear elsewhere as a scan target and
#   not as personal history
# API key prefix (the fixed leading characters your provider always uses)
# Your absolute home-directory path prefix
